    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is powered by a core of high-floor, high-upside plays against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the charge with an elite 83.29 score; his matchup against Arrighetti is bolstered by a massive 16% SP skill edge and a slow pitcher delivery profile that significantly enhances his stolen base potential\u2014the ultimate priority for our squad. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) are primary targets, both benefiting from sub-5.00 xERA opposing starters and advantageous spots in the two-hole. **Jacob Wilson** also provides immense value (74.07) batting leadoff against Littell, where a 10% park factor bump and a 19% SP skill advantage propel him into \"Strong\" start territory.\n\nWe see notable platoon and park-adjusted spikes for **Cole Carrigg**, whose 71.23 score is largely driven by a 14% park factor advantage at his home venue, and **Sam Antonacci**, whose position atop the order against Bieber provides the necessary volume to compensate for the veteran starter's presence. Our most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung** (43.31); while his 43.31 score cleared the baseline floor, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Miguel Vargas** and the surrounding outfield depth. **Josh Jung** remains a high-risk hold given the matchup against Murphy, O, who remains a statistically difficult arm to solve. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Luis Lara** (42.27) and **Heliot Ramos** (45.19); both are currently hovering in the \"Marginal\" bucket due to stiffer SP matchups and less-than-ideal park conditions, but they remain in the lineup to ensure we are capitalizing on all available plate appearances in our quest to close the gap in category scoring.",
